{"1-10":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":4,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"kiriathaim-h7156g","name":"Kiriathaim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"misgab-h4869b","name":"Misgab","kind":"place","brief":"In Moab","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"nebo-h5015a","name":"Nebo","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"heshbon-h2809","name":"Heshbon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"madmen-h4086","name":"Madmen","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"horonaim-h2773","name":"Horonaim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"luhith-h3872","name":"Luhith","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5}],"words":[{"base":"H4124","lemma":"מוֹאָב","tr":"mo·av","gloss":"Moab","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":181},{"base":"H2773","lemma":"חֹרֹנַיִם","tr":"cho·ro·na·yim","gloss":"Horonaim","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H6818","lemma":"צְעָקָה","tr":"tsa·a·qah","gloss":"cry","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":21},{"base":"H1065","lemma":"בְּכִי","tr":"be·khi","gloss":"weeping","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":30},{"base":"H7667","lemma":"שֶׁ֫בֶר","tr":"she·ver","gloss":"breaking","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":45},{"base":"H7703","lemma":"שָׁדַד","tr":"sha·dad","gloss":"to ruin","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":57},{"base":"H0779","lemma":"אָרַר","tr":"a·rar","gloss":"to curse","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":63},{"base":"H4422","lemma":"מָלַט","tr":"ma·lat","gloss":"to escape","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":95},{"base":"H3920","lemma":"לָכַד","tr":"la·khad","gloss":"to capture","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":121},{"base":"H0954","lemma":"בּוֹשׁ","tr":"bush","gloss":"be ashamed","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":127}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1KI","chapter":20,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"And the prophet said to the king, “This is what the LORD says: ‘Because you have let slip from your hand the man I had devoted to destruction, your life will be exchanged for his life, and your people for his people.’”","from":10},{"book":"1SA","chapter":15,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Now go and attack the Amalekites and devote to destruction all that belongs to them. Do not spare them, but put to death men and women, children and infants, oxen and sheep, camels and donkeys.’”","from":10},{"book":"JDG","chapter":5,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"‘Curse Meroz,’ says the angel of the LORD. ‘Bitterly curse her inhabitants; for they did not come to help the LORD, to help the LORD against the mighty.’","from":10},{"book":"1SA","chapter":15,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Saul and his troops spared Agag, along with the best of the sheep and cattle, the fat calves and lambs, and the best of everything else. They were unwilling to devote them to distruction, but they devoted to destruction all that was despised and worthless.","from":10},{"book":"NUM","chapter":31,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"But Moses was angry with the officers of the army—the commanders of thousands and commanders of hundreds—who were returning from the battle.","from":10},{"book":"NUM","chapter":31,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"but spare for yourselves every girl who has never had relations with a man.","from":10},{"book":"2KI","chapter":13,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"But the man of God was angry with him and said, “You should have struck the ground five or six times. Then you would have struck down Aram until you had put an end to it. But now you will strike down Aram only three times.”","from":10},{"book":"JER","chapter":50,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The LORD has opened His armory and brought out His weapons of wrath, for this is the work of the Lord GOD of Hosts in the land of the Chaldeans.","from":10}],"notes":[{"id":"jer-48-moab-ammon","title":"Moab and Ammon humbled","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[]},"11-20":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":6,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"bethel-h1008g","name":"Bethel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"dibon-h1769g","name":"Dibon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"aroer-h6177h","name":"Aroer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"arnon-h0769","name":"Arnon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20}],"words":[{"base":"H4124","lemma":"מוֹאָב","tr":"mo·av","gloss":"Moab","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":181},{"base":"H7703","lemma":"שָׁדַד","tr":"sha·dad","gloss":"to ruin","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":57},{"base":"H6808","lemma":"צָעָה","tr":"tsa·ah","gloss":"to march","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H0954","lemma":"בּוֹשׁ","tr":"bush","gloss":"be ashamed","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":127},{"base":"H7324","lemma":"רִיק","tr":"ruq","gloss":"to empty","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":19},{"base":"H3627","lemma":"כְּלִי","tr":"ke·li","gloss":"article","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":325},{"base":"H0349","lemma":"אֵיךְ","tr":"ekh","gloss":"how?","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":82},{"base":"H1008","lemma":"בֵּֽיתְ־אֵל","tr":"bet-el","gloss":"Bethel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":142},{"base":"H3427","lemma":"יָשַׁב","tr":"ya·shav","gloss":"to dwell","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1079},{"base":"H5002","lemma":"נְאֻם","tr":"ne·um","gloss":"utterance","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":376}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ZEP","chapter":1,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And at that time I will search Jerusalem with lamps and punish the men settled in complacency, who say to themselves, ‘The LORD will do nothing, either good or bad.’","from":11},{"book":"NUM","chapter":21,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But we have overthrown them; Heshbon is destroyed as far as Dibon. We demolished them as far as Nophah, which reaches to Medeba.”","from":18},{"book":"DEU","chapter":2,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"From Aroer on the rim of the Arnon Valley, along with the city in the valley, even as far as Gilead, not one city had walls too high for us. The LORD our God gave us all of them.","from":19},{"book":"ISA","chapter":47,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“Go down and sit in the dust, O Virgin Daughter of Babylon. Sit on the ground without a throne, O Daughter of the Chaldeans! For you will no longer be called tender or delicate.","from":18},{"book":"JER","chapter":46,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"As surely as I live, declares the King, whose name is the LORD of Hosts, there will come one who is like Tabor among the mountains and like Carmel by the sea.","from":15},{"book":"JER","chapter":50,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Kill all her young bulls; let them go down to the slaughter. Woe to them, for their day has come— the time of their punishment.","from":15},{"book":"ZEC","chapter":1,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"but I am fiercely angry with the nations that are at ease. For I was a little angry, but they have added to the calamity.’","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then she went off and sat down nearby, about a bowshot away, for she said, “I cannot bear to watch the boy die!” And as she sat nearby, she lifted up her voice and wept.","from":18}],"notes":[{"id":"jer-48-moab-ammon","title":"Moab and Ammon humbled","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[]},"21-28":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":27}],"places":[{"id":"holon-h2473h","name":"Holon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"jahaz-h3096","name":"Jahaz","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"mephaath-h4158","name":"Mephaath","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"diblathaim-h5963","name":"Diblathaim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"dibon-h1769g","name":"Dibon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"nebo-h5015a","name":"Nebo","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"kiriathaim-h7156g","name":"Kiriathaim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"baal-meon-h1186","name":"Baal-meon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"beth-gamul-h1014","name":"Beth-gamul","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":4,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"bezer-h1221g","name":"Bezer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24}],"words":[{"base":"H4124","lemma":"מוֹאָב","tr":"mo·av","gloss":"Moab","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":181},{"base":"H1010","lemma":"בֵּית מְעוֹן","tr":"bet ba·al me·on","gloss":"Beth-meon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1014","lemma":"בֵּית גָּמוּל","tr":"bet ga·mul","gloss":"Beth-gamul","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1015","lemma":"בֵּית דִּבְלָתָ֑יִם","tr":"bet div·la·ta·yim","gloss":"Beth-diblathaim","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H7814","lemma":"שְׂחֹק","tr":"se·choq","gloss":"laughter","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":15},{"base":"H2473","lemma":"חֹלוֹן","tr":"cho·lon","gloss":"Holon","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H4158","lemma":"מֵיפַ֫עַת","tr":"mo·pha·at","gloss":"Mephaath","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H6892","lemma":"קֵא","tr":"qe","gloss":"vomit","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H7152","lemma":"קְרִיּוֹת","tr":"qe·riy·yot","gloss":"Kerioth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H7077","lemma":"קִנֵּן","tr":"qa·nan","gloss":"to make a nest","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":13,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"to Heshbon and all its cities on the plateau, including Dibon, Bamoth-baal, Beth-baal-meon,","from":23},{"book":"JOS","chapter":13,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Jahaz, Kedemoth, Mephaath,","from":21},{"book":"PSA","chapter":75,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“All the horns of the wicked I will cut off, but the horns of the righteous will be exalted.”","from":25},{"book":"JER","chapter":2,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"As the thief is ashamed when he is caught, so the house of Israel is disgraced. They, their kings, their officials, their priests, and their prophets","from":27},{"book":"AMO","chapter":2,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So I will send fire against Moab to consume the citadels of Kerioth. Moab will die in tumult, amid war cries and the sound of the ramʼs horn.","from":24},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In the fourteenth year, Chedorlaomer and the kings allied with him went out and defeated the Rephaites in Ashteroth-karnaim, the Zuzites in Ham, the Emites in Shaveh-kiriathaim,","from":23},{"book":"EXO","chapter":5,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"But Pharaoh replied, “Who is the LORD that I should obey His voice and let Israel go? I do not know the LORD, and I will not let Israel go.”","from":26},{"book":"EXO","chapter":9,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Still, you lord it over My people and do not allow them to go.","from":26}],"notes":[{"id":"jer-48-moab-ammon","title":"Moab and Ammon humbled","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[]},"29-39":{"people":[],"places":[{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":7,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"kir-h7024a","name":"Kir","kind":"place","brief":"In Moab","count":2,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"jazer-h3270g","name":"Jazer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"jazer-sea-h3270h","name":"Jazer Sea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"sibmah-h7643h","name":"Sibmah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"eglath-shelishiyah-h5697b","name":"Eglath-shelishiyah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"elealeh-h0500","name":"Elealeh","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"heshbon-h2809","name":"Heshbon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"horonaim-h2773","name":"Horonaim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"jahaz-h3096","name":"Jahaz","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"nimrim-h5249","name":"Nimrim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"zoar-h6820","name":"Zoar","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34}],"words":[{"base":"H4124","lemma":"מוֹאָב","tr":"mo·av","gloss":"Moab","lang":"h","inPassage":10,"uses":181},{"base":"H7025","lemma":"קִיר חֶרֶשׂ","tr":"qir che·re·s","gloss":"Kir-hareseth","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":10},{"base":"H1959","lemma":"הֵידָד","tr":"he·dad","gloss":"shout","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":7},{"base":"H3651","lemma":"כֵּן","tr":"ken","gloss":"right","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":765},{"base":"H2485","lemma":"חָלִיל","tr":"cha·lil","gloss":"flute","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H3270","lemma":"יַעְזֵר","tr":"ya·a·zer","gloss":"Jazer","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":13},{"base":"H5002","lemma":"נְאֻם","tr":"ne·um","gloss":"utterance","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":376},{"base":"H3213","lemma":"יָלַל","tr":"ya·lal","gloss":"to wail","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":30},{"base":"H1993","lemma":"הָמָה","tr":"ha·mah","gloss":"to roar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":34},{"base":"H1347","lemma":"גָּאוֹן","tr":"ga·on","gloss":"pride","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":49}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2KI","chapter":3,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"They destroyed the cities, and each man threw stones on every good field until it was covered. They stopped up every spring and cut down every good tree. Only Kir-haraseth was left with stones in place, but men with slings surrounded it and attacked it as well.","from":31},{"book":"ISA","chapter":15,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Dibon goes up to its temple to weep at its high places. Moab wails over Nebo, as well as over Medeba. Every head is shaved, every beard is cut off.","from":35},{"book":"ISA","chapter":15,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Heshbon and Elealeh cry out; their voices are heard as far as Jahaz. Therefore the soldiers of Moab cry out; their souls tremble within.","from":34},{"book":"ISA","chapter":15,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"My heart cries out over Moab; her fugitives flee as far as Zoar, as far as Eglath-shelishiyah. With weeping they ascend the slope of Luhith; they lament their destruction on the road to Horonaim.","from":31},{"book":"ISA","chapter":15,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The waters of Nimrim are dried up, and the grass is withered; the vegetation is gone, and the greenery is no more.","from":34},{"book":"ISA","chapter":15,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So they carry their wealth and belongings over the Brook of the Willows.","from":36},{"book":"ISA","chapter":16,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"We have heard of Moabʼs pomposity, his exceeding pride and conceit, his overflowing arrogance. But his boasting is empty.","from":29},{"book":"ISA","chapter":16,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"For the fields of Heshbon have withered, along with the grapevines of Sibmah. The rulers of the nations have trampled its choicest vines, which had reached as far as Jazer and spread toward the desert. Their shoots had spread out and passed over the sea.","from":32}],"notes":[{"id":"jer-48-moab-ammon","title":"Moab and Ammon humbled","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[]},"40-47":{"people":[{"id":"sihon-h5511","name":"Sihon","kind":"person","brief":"Amorite king","count":1,"firstVerse":45}],"places":[{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":8,"firstVerse":40},{"id":"kiriathaim-h7156g","name":"Kiriathaim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":41},{"id":"heshbon-h2809","name":"Heshbon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":45}],"words":[{"base":"H4124","lemma":"מוֹאָב","tr":"mo·av","gloss":"Moab","lang":"h","inPassage":9,"uses":181},{"base":"H6354","lemma":"פַּ֫חַת","tr":"pa·chat","gloss":"pit","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":10},{"base":"H6341","lemma":"פַּח","tr":"pach","gloss":"snare","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":27},{"base":"H5002","lemma":"נְאֻם","tr":"ne·um","gloss":"utterance","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":376},{"base":"H2809","lemma":"חֶשְׁבּוֹן","tr":"chesh·bon","gloss":"Heshbon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":38},{"base":"H6343","lemma":"פַּ֫חַד","tr":"pa·chad","gloss":"dread","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":49},{"base":"H3920","lemma":"לָכַד","tr":"la·khad","gloss":"to capture","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":121},{"base":"H5127","lemma":"נוּס","tr":"nus","gloss":"to flee","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":159},{"base":"H1675","lemma":"דָּאָה","tr":"da·ah","gloss":"to fly","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H7152","lemma":"קְרִיּוֹת","tr":"qe·riy·yot","gloss":"Kerioth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":24,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I see him, but not now; I behold him, but not near. A star will come forth from Jacob, and a scepter will arise from Israel. He will crush the skulls of Moab and strike down all the sons of Sheth.","from":45},{"book":"DEU","chapter":28,"verse":49,"verseEnd":49,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The LORD will bring a nation from afar, from the ends of the earth, to swoop down upon you like an eagle—a nation whose language you will not understand,","from":40},{"book":"ISA","chapter":8,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"It will pour into Judah, swirling and sweeping over it, reaching up to the neck; its spreading streams will cover your entire land, O Immanuel!","from":40},{"book":"JER","chapter":49,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Yet afterward I will restore the Ammonites from captivity,” declares the LORD.","from":47},{"book":"JER","chapter":49,"verse":39,"verseEnd":39,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“Yet in the last days, I will restore Elam from captivity,” declares the LORD.","from":47},{"book":"NUM","chapter":21,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"For a fire went out from Heshbon, a blaze from the city of Sihon. It consumed Ar of Moab, the rulers of Arnonʼs heights.","from":45},{"book":"NUM","chapter":21,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Woe to you, O Moab! You are destroyed, O people of Chemosh! He gave up his sons as refugees, and his daughters into captivity to Sihon king of the Amorites.","from":46},{"book":"NUM","chapter":24,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now I am going back to my people, but come, let me warn you what this people will do to your people in the days to come.”","from":47}],"notes":[{"id":"jer-48-moab-ammon","title":"Moab and Ammon humbled","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[]}}